            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Also, one thing to add. Since this mentioned MiniMax, the goal of its [setting up steps](https://nvim-mini.org/MiniMax/#setting-up) is to have a working config for any supported Neovim version *indefinitely*. So in theory even in case 'mini.deps' is removed from 'mini.nvim', setting up MiniMax with Neovim=0.10 would still work. Yes, it will check out not the latest available versions and without custom tweaks, but still.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Also, one thing to add. Since this mentioned MiniMax, the goal of its <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/MiniMax/#setting-up\" rel=\"nofollow\">setting up steps</a> is to have a working config for any supported Neovim version <em>indefinitely</em>. So in theory even in case 'mini.deps' is removed from 'mini.nvim', setting up MiniMax with Neovim=0.10 would still work. Yes, it will check out not the latest available versions and without custom tweaks, but still.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Also, one thing to add. Since this mentioned MiniMax, the goal of its setting up steps is to have a working config for any supported Neovim version indefinitely. So in theory even in case 'mini.deps' is removed from 'mini.nvim', setting up MiniMax with Neovim=0.10 would still work. Yes, it will check out not the latest available versions and without custom tweaks, but still.",
